  "body": [
    "Register for Fall Programming! Session runs now - Nov 8.",
    "PLAY PLAY submenu Programs Private Lessons Adult Camps Summer Camps Book a Court Free30 Dave Bailey Programs",
    "EVENTS EVENTS submenu Calendar 2026 BNP Paribas World Team Cup",
    "ABOUT ABOUT submenu Meet Our Team Contact Us Sponsors & Partners USTA National Campus Scholarship",
    "WATCH WATCH submenu Watch Live Record Your Match",
    "VISIT VISIT submenu Hotel Booking Sustainability Health & Wellness Shop",
    "Home >",
    "Play >",
    "Tennis >",
    "Junior Programming Welcome Letter",
    "The USTA National Campus is pleased to be a part of your child’s tennis journey and share our passion for the sport!",
    "At the heart of our programs, we aim to:",
    "Build character and life skills through the game of tennis.",
    "Inspire a love for the sport that lasts a lifetime.",
    "Create opportunities for all players to practice, play, and grow.",
    "Guide each player’s journey—whether they’re just starting or chasing big goals.",
    "Provide top-quality coaching in a fun and supportive environment.",
    "View our Junior Programs Overview!",
    "We believe in creating a positive, supportive, and fun learning environment. Here’s how players and parents can help make that happen:",
    "For Players",
    "Show respect for your coaches and fellow players.",
    "Encourage and support others on and off the court.",
    "Always give your best effort and stay engaged.",
    "Most importantly—have fun while learning and improving!",
    "For Parents",
    "Support your child’s tennis journey by focusing on effort and long-term growth.",
    "Avoid coaching from the sidelines—too many voices can be distracting.",
    "Every player develops at their own pace—celebrate progress, not comparisons.",
    "Match play opportunities are included with your full session registration. This includes the following programs:",
    "Red Ball Club, Red Ball Plus",
    "Youth 1",
    "Orange Ball Club, Orange Ball Plus, Youth 2",
    "Junior Varsity, Varsity, Collegiate",
    "Makeup classes provide players with the opportunity to attend a session they missed due to sickness, travel, etc. These classes are scheduled based on availability and must be used within the same session.",
    "Join us for Parent Information sessions during our Friday Match Play.",
    "RETURNING FALL 2026",
    "Community Day | Saturday, September 19",
    "Walk-ups are not accepted, and spots are limited. Makeups are not offered for missed drop-ins or match play registrations. Weather-related cancellations do not qualify for makeups; however, players enrolled in the full session will receive rain credits to their family account for future use. Drop-in participants will receive a refund for weather cancellations but are not eligible for makeup classes. Credits or refunds will not be provided if you are unable to attend your scheduled makeup class.",
    "All players are encouraged to become a USTA member; it is FREE for junior players. It allows you to register for sanctioned tournaments and build your rating. Learn how to create your account.",
    "Player progression to the next level class in our Program pathway depends on several factors: age (chronological vs. biological), how often they play, maturity, etc. We focus on having players fully develop skills before advancing to ensure they are successful and have confidence at the next level. It is very common for players to be in a class for more than one session; this does not mean that your child is not progressing! Rather, we are cementing skills. Our coaching methods are designed to challenge each player individually. Read Our Move-Up Policy",
    "🔴 Red Ball Programs: Bailey Robinson, bailey.robinson@usta.com",
    "🟠🟢 Orange and Green Ball Programs: Jenny Booth, jenny.booth@usta.com",
    "🟡 Yellow Ball Programs: Sean Bleau, sean.bleau@usta.com",
    "10",
